# Coinnibal game server on the VPS: /opt/elymum/.env (mode 600, never committed). No real secret belongs in this
# example file. Every key is explained in apps/server/.env.example; deploy/vps/README.md section 4 lists what the owner
# sets.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around "=". docker compose reads this file and expands "$NAME"
# inside unquoted values: put a value containing "$" in single quotes ('like$this').
#
# Set by docker-compose.yml, ignored here: DATA_DIR=/data, PORT=8787, HOST=0.0.0.0, TRUST_PROXY=1,
# TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1 (Caddy is the one proxy in front and sets X-Forwarded-For itself).
#
# Also ignored here, always: CHAIN_ID, EVM_RPC_URL, EVM_RPC_URLS, RPC_MAX_RPS, GAME_ACCESS, WEB_DIST, PUBLIC_URL,
# PUBLIC_RPC_URL, TESTNET_RPC_URL, EXPLORER_URL, ARENA_ADDRESS, NFT_ADDRESS, TOKEN_ADDRESS, JOURNAL_ABANDON_CONTRACT.
# An older .env (filled from the Elysium / Render setup) may still hold stale values of them, so docker-compose.yml
# overrides them. The chain, the RPCs, the request budget and the game access come from the COINNIBAL_* keys below,
# the site's origin from SITE_DOMAIN (or COINNIBAL_PUBLIC_URL). Each COINNIBAL_* key still accepts its ELYMUM_* name of
# before the rename (a .env written then keeps working); the COINNIBAL_* name wins when both are set (README
# "Settings").

# ───────── This VPS ─────────
# The game server's own domain (Caddy gets its HTTPS certificate). DNS: an A record to this server's IP.
# The live server's is game.elymum.io: a record under elymum.io, kept from before the rename (its DNS record and
# certificate exist); game.coinnibal.fun once that A record exists.
GAME_DOMAIN=game.elymum.io
# Caddy's config: Caddyfile (default) or Caddyfile.cloudflare once GAME_DOMAIN is proxied by Cloudflare
# (README "Cloudflare in front"). Then: coinnibal-compose up -d caddy
# CADDY_CONFIG=Caddyfile.cloudflare

# The site's domain (default coinnibal.fun; Caddy serves it, www redirects to it). The server's PUBLIC_URL, the SITE's
# origin (where players sign in), not this server's, is https://<SITE_DOMAIN>: wallet sign-ins (SIWE) are bound to it,
# the NFT metadata links start with it, and a browser that opens a page of the game domain is sent there.
# COINNIBAL_PUBLIC_URL (old name ELYMUM_PUBLIC_URL) overrides that origin.
# SITE_DOMAIN=coinnibal.fun
# COINNIBAL_PUBLIC_URL=

# ───────── Required ─────────
NODE_ENV=production
# Checked by install.sh (it must not be empty), ignored by docker-compose.yml: set SITE_DOMAIN or COINNIBAL_PUBLIC_URL
# above to change the site's origin.
PUBLIC_URL=https://coinnibal.fun
# The site's origin that calls this server (a comma-separated list; the server always adds the brand's own sites).
CORS_ORIGIN=https://coinnibal.fun
# Owner / admin wallets, comma-separated 0x addresses. Empty: nobody is admin.
ADMIN_WALLETS=
# Login token secret: openssl rand -hex 32 (at least 32 bytes: the mainnet refuses to start with less). Empty: the
# generated DATA_DIR/auth-secret (in the backups too).
AUTH_SECRET=
# The server's signing key: auto (DATA_DIR/server-key.json, carried by the backups), a 0x hex key, or a file path.
# Two servers must never run with the same key.
SERVER_PRIVATE_KEY=auto
# Admin sessions last this many minutes (default 120) and are never extended; POST /api/admin/auth/revoke ends them.
# ADMIN_TOKEN_TTL_MIN=120
# The backup and the migration settings hand out the server key: on the mainnet they are off unless this is 1 (set it
# only for the time of a move, then remove it). On a testnet they work (0 turns them off).
# ADMIN_SECRET_EXPORT=

# ───────── Chain: Robinhood Chain only (optional: unset = the live testnet) ─────────
# The network: 46630 = Robinhood Chain Testnet (the default when unset), 4663 = Robinhood Chain (mainnet). Anything
# else refuses to start.
# COINNIBAL_CHAIN_ID=46630
# The server's RPCs, in order, comma-separated: a provider first (it may hold an API key; never sent to browsers), the
# public RPC as fallback. Every one must serve the chain above. Unset: https://rpc.testnet.chain.robinhood.com.
# Mainnet (README "RPC"):
#   COINNIBAL_RPC_URLS=https://robinhood-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/<key>,https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# COINNIBAL_RPC_URLS=
# The request budget: calls per second, one per COINNIBAL_RPC_URLS entry ("25,4": Alchemy, then the public RPC); default 4
# COINNIBAL_RPC_MAX_RPS=25,4
# RPC_BURST=8
# The browser RPC (the public RPC of the list), the explorer and the contract addresses (the /admin registry) are not
# set here: docker-compose.yml leaves them to the server.
# Only after reviewing a quarantined journal (journal.json.corrupt-*): 1
STALE_SWEEP_ACK=
# Token arenas on/off, and an optional list of arena ids (empty = every enabled arena on chain)
STAKE_ENABLED=true
STAKE_ARENA_IDS=
# Display symbol of the game token in the game (default: tokens). The visitor site and /docs always say tokens.
# Display only; quote a value that contains $.
# TOKEN_SYMBOL=tokens
# The project's X handle by default (no @; default coinnibalfun). Set X_HANDLE only to use another account
# (docs/OPERATIONS.md, "The name: Coinnibal (formerly Elymum)"); the admin's Settings, X handle, can also change it at any time.
# X_HANDLE=
# Unplayed tickets are cancelled with their full entry fee after this many seconds (default 900; at once in an arena
# that is closed, paused or closing for a re-price). Ticket ages are measured on the chain's clock.
# STALE_SESSION_AFTER_S=900
# Eaten tickets (payout 0) wait this many seconds for each other and go out in one settle batch (default 6, 0 to 30)
# DEATH_SETTLE_BATCH_S=6
# Blocks per eth_getLogs request (default 50000; lower it if the RPC limits log ranges)
# LOG_CHUNK_BLOCKS=50000
# Testnet ETH faucet linked from /faucet (default: faucet.testnet.chain.robinhood.com)
# GAS_FAUCET_URL=

# ───────── Contract pins: the contracts the site trusts (optional override) ─────────
# The site trusts only the contracts the owner wallet signed for: after a deploy, /admin asks the owner for one free
# signature (Setup -> "Site pins"), the server stores it and every browser checks it against the owner wallet built
# into the site. Nothing to set here. Optional override: these lines pin addresses in the build itself (passed as
# VITE_ARENA_ADDRESS, VITE_NFT_ADDRESS and VITE_TOKEN_ADDRESS on the chain of COINNIBAL_CHAIN_ID; a pin here wins over
# the signed one) and need a rebuild: coinnibal-compose up -d --build app (README section 4). COINNIBAL_OWNER_WALLET
# replaces the built-in owner wallet (0x08b2b32E932D5f429073a441E6eFd8e3D42369b2).
# COINNIBAL_PIN_ARENA=
# COINNIBAL_PIN_NFT=
# COINNIBAL_PIN_TOKEN=
# COINNIBAL_OWNER_WALLET=

# ───────── The server key's gas ─────────
# Low when under the floor, else by runway at the last day's spend: a warning under 7 days, an alert under 2.
# GAS_FLOOR_ETH=0.002
# GAS_RUNWAY_WARN_DAYS=7
# GAS_RUNWAY_CRITICAL_DAYS=2

# ───────── Health and alerts ─────────
# /api/health answers 503 above this many due settlements, or when the oldest is older than this (seconds)
# HEALTH_MAX_PENDING=400
# HEALTH_MAX_PENDING_AGE_S=900
# Telegram alerts (alert.sh, every minute): @BotFather's bot token and your chat id. Empty: the journal only.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ───────── Deploys and backups ─────────
# 1: deploy only commits CI marked green (the ci-green-<branch> tag); without it the branch head is deployed when
# no marker exists yet
# COINNIBAL_REQUIRE_CI=1
# An rclone remote of type crypt for an encrypted offsite copy of every backup (README "Backups"), and how long the
# copies are kept there
# (elymum-offsite: the name the README gave the remote before the rename; a remote set up then keeps it, any name works)
# BACKUP_RCLONE_REMOTE=elymum-offsite:
# BACKUP_RCLONE_KEEP_DAYS=30

# ───────── Game access (optional: unset = site, the /admin → Settings switch decides) ─────────
# Set it only to override that switch: public | holders | admins | maintenance (closed)
# COINNIBAL_GAME_ACCESS=site

# ───────── NFT mint ─────────
# Mint target in US cents (default 100 = $1) and the ETH/USD feed
MINT_USD_CENTS=100
# GAS_PRICE_URL=https://api.hyperliquid.xyz/info
# Emblem collection (docs/NFT-DESIGN.md): size (= max supply) and art style; the seed is generated and committed on first boot
# NFT_COLLECTION_SIZE=3333
# NFT_ART_STYLE=vector

# ───────── Capacity (8 vCPU, 16 GB RAM) ─────────
# Room worker threads: the rooms (simulation, practice bots of free custom rooms and test arenas, snapshots) run on this many cores; the
# main thread keeps the sockets, HTTP, the chain and the journal. 5 on 8 vCPU (two cores stay for Caddy, Docker and the
# host). Unset: one per core but one. Measured: 500 players use about 1.7 cores in all.
GAME_WORKERS=5
# A room worker silent this long (seconds) is stopped: its tickets are settled from the journal, as after
# a restart, and it starts again (default 10)
# GAME_WORKER_HANG_S=10
# WebSockets in all (about 1 MB each with the rooms; 1500 fits 16 GB with room to spare). Guests (not signed in) use at
# most 80 % of them and are limited per IP and per /24; signed-in players are not limited per IP (carrier NAT), and a
# player with a live arena coin always gets back in.
MAX_CONNECTIONS=1500
MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_IP=8
# MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_SUBNET=48
# Humans per practice room, per private room, per arena instance
# PRACTICE_CAPACITY=40
# PRIVATE_ROOM_CAPACITY=20
# ARENA_INSTANCE_CAP=50
# Arena round clock in seconds (defaults 300 and 60): leave unset in production. ROUND_SECONDS is the full play
# ROUND_SECONDS=300
# ROUND_JOIN_CLOSE_SECONDS=60
# The break after each bell before joins open again, added on top of the play (default 30: a 5:30 cycle)
# ROUND_BREAK_SECONDS=30

# ───────── Never on this server ─────────
# DEV_FAKE_CHAIN and DEV_FAKE_TOKEN are for local development only.
# The VPS serves the site itself: WEB_DIST is /app/web (the bundled client, strict CSP) unless COINNIBAL_WEB_DIST says
# otherwise; leave it unset.
# COINNIBAL_WEB_DIST=
